+The <i>Provenance.target</i> MAY point at a specific element within the targeted resource using the <a href="[%extensions-location%]StructureDefinition-targetElement.html">target element extension</a> or <a href="[%extensions-location%]StructureDefinition-targetPath.html">target path extension</a>. For example when updating a Patient resource with a new official name, such as shown in <a href="provenance-example1.html">example 1</a>, where the Provenance is indicating that the official name was provided by the Patient themselves. These same extensions can be used on other references, such as <i>Provenance.entity.what</i>, when a target resource was derived from a specific element in a source resource, as shown in <a href="provenance-example7.html">example 7</a>.
